-- Cases for wirc-regs-seat-employer.l4 (the employer's and self-insurer's seat). Expected values are worked by hand
-- from the deposited text of the Regulations (S.R. No. 35/2024, version 001) and the 2013 Act.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wirc-regs-seat-employer`

§ `Regulation 13 — reimbursement`

-- Notified 10 March 2027: 30 days after (not counting the 10th) is 9 April 2027 (21 days left in March + 9).
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority reimburse me` TRUE (Date 10 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 4 2027)
-- Notified 15 January 2027: 14 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority reimburse me` TRUE (Date 15 1 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 2 2027)
-- Notified 31 January 2028 (a leap year): 1 March 2028 (29 days of February, then 1).
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority reimburse me` TRUE (Date 31 1 2028) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2028)
-- Not required to pay first: s 179(5) does not apply.
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority reimburse me` FALSE (Date 10 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Reimbursed on the last day: no interest. The day after: interest.
#ASSERT `Is the Authority liable to pay me interest on my weekly payment` TRUE (Date 10 3 2027) TRUE (Date 9 4 2027) (Date 1 5 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Authority liable to pay me interest on my weekly payment` TRUE (Date 10 3 2027) TRUE (Date 10 4 2027) (Date 1 5 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not yet reimbursed: on the last day, no interest yet; two days later, interest.
#ASSERT `Is the Authority liable to pay me interest on my weekly payment` TRUE (Date 10 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 9 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Authority liable to pay me interest on my weekly payment` TRUE (Date 10 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 11 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not required to pay first.
#ASSERT `Is the Authority liable to pay me interest on my weekly payment` FALSE (Date 10 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 11 4 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 14 — quarterly contributions until 31 December 2024`

-- A $1,000,000; B $10,000,000; C $1,000,000,000 (share 1%); D $3,000,000 + $1,500,000 + $500,000 = $5,000,000.
-- B/C x D = $50,000; A x B/C = $10,000; ($50,000 - $10,000) x 0.6 = $24,000; + $10,000 = $34,000.
#ASSERT `What is my quarterly self-insurer contribution under regulation 14` (Date 1 10 2024) 1000000 10000000 1000000000 3000000 1500000 500000 EQUALS JUST 34000
-- On 31 December 2024 (the last day): the same.
#ASSERT `What is my quarterly self-insurer contribution under regulation 14` (Date 31 12 2024) 1000000 10000000 1000000000 3000000 1500000 500000 EQUALS JUST 34000
-- From 1 January 2025: regulation 14 no longer gives an amount.
#ASSERT `What is my quarterly self-insurer contribution under regulation 14` (Date 1 1 2025) 1000000 10000000 1000000000 3000000 1500000 500000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A only (D equal to A): 60% applies to nothing, the full share of A: $10,000.
#ASSERT `What is my quarterly self-insurer contribution under regulation 14` (Date 1 7 2024) 1000000 10000000 1000000000 1000000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 10000
-- No remuneration total: no share can be worked out.
#ASSERT `What is my quarterly self-insurer contribution under regulation 14` (Date 1 10 2024) 1000000 10000000 0 3000000 1500000 500000 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 15 — contributions from 1 January 2025`

-- A = $20,000,000 + $4,000,000 + $1,000,000 + $1,000,000 = $26,000,000; B $2,000,000,000; C $40,000,000 (2%).
-- A/B x C = $520,000; 25% = $130,000.
#ASSERT `What is my self-insurer contribution under regulation 15` (Date 1 1 2025) 20000000 4000000 1000000 1000000 2000000000 40000000 EQUALS JUST 130000
#ASSERT `What is my self-insurer contribution under regulation 15` (Date 2 1 2026) 20000000 4000000 1000000 1000000 2000000000 40000000 EQUALS JUST 130000
-- Before 1 January 2025: regulation 15 does not yet apply.
#ASSERT `What is my self-insurer contribution under regulation 15` (Date 31 12 2024) 20000000 4000000 1000000 1000000 2000000000 40000000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- No remuneration total.
#ASSERT `What is my self-insurer contribution under regulation 15` (Date 1 1 2026) 20000000 4000000 1000000 1000000 0 40000000 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 388(3) — due dates`

#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 6 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 2 2027)
#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 1 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 11 2026)
#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 15 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 2 2027)
#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 2 2 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 5 2027)
#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2027)
#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 1 8 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2027)
#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 2 8 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 11 2027)
#ASSERT `When is my next self-insurer contribution due` (Date 6 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 388(5) — recovery of a contribution not paid within 14 days`

-- Due 1 February 2027; 14 days after is 15 February 2027.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can my contribution be recovered as a debt` (Date 1 2 2027) TRUE (Date 15 2 2027) (Date 1 3 2027)))
#ASSERT `Can my contribution be recovered as a debt` (Date 1 2 2027) TRUE (Date 16 2 2027) (Date 1 3 2027)
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can my contribution be recovered as a debt` (Date 1 2 2027) TRUE (Date 1 2 2027) (Date 1 3 2027)))
-- Paid before the due date.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can my contribution be recovered as a debt` (Date 1 2 2027) TRUE (Date 20 1 2027) (Date 1 3 2027)))
-- Unpaid: on 15 February not yet; on 16 February yes.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can my contribution be recovered as a debt` (Date 1 2 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 15 2 2027)))
#ASSERT `Can my contribution be recovered as a debt` (Date 1 2 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 16 2 2027)
